WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:02.869 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  surrounded by bailiffs and medics  sixteen-year-old rory hooper emerged to  gray skies above houston station  for his moment in the sun  [Applause]  we filmed the teenager as his three  weeks underground  came to an end he said he'd loved his  experience  but was leaving to conserve supplies for  the remaining protesters  enabling them to stay longer rory's  mother said she was very proud of her  son  but thought he was looking forward to  some home-cooked food  at 16 rory hooper is one of the youngest  activists  ever to have gone underground for his  cause if not the youngest so medics will  be keen  to get him checked out and see what kind  of impact  three weeks in a tunnel has had on him  rory went below ground with his father  daniel  a veteran environmentalist known as  swampy who first became famous for  digging tunnels to stop a road project  in the 90s  and now remains beneath the gardens in  front of houston station  with four others a chip off the old  block  rory said his actions might seem extreme  but he felt it was the only way to raise  the profile of the campaign  to stop the development of hs2 in an  ecological emergency  see around the world that young people  understand the implications  they understand that they're being  robbed of their future and they're  saying  enough is enough with four tunnelers now  gone  below ground the rest are still playing  cat and  mouse with bailiffs the down south  in a video message sent to sky news one  of the activists  said a tactic of separating the group is  now being used  within three different groups now across  these tunnels um  so effectively they split this longer  tunnel in in half  so i'm somewhat on my own dealing with  that but i'm okay  our spirits are still strong the houston  tunnelers say they'll keep going for as  long as they can  sixteen-year-old rory hooper says he's  been  on an amazing journey which has now  ended with his arrest  lisa holland sky news houston station

